    "storyEn": "<p>Prophet Idris (AS) was among the earliest prophets after Adam and Sheeth (Seth). Classical traditions record that he was the first human to write with a pen, master astronomy, study the measurements of time, and sew garments instead of wearing animal skins.</p>\n    <p>He was a man of steadfast truthfulness and continuous remembrance of Allah. The Holy Quran pays tribute to his elevated status: <em>'And mention in the Book, Idris. Indeed, he was a man of truth and a prophet. And We raised him to a high station.'</em> (19:56-57). When Prophet Muhammad ﷺ ascended during the Miraj, he met Idris (AS) in the fourth heaven.</p>",
